WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.700
- Narrator: In the early 1960s

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:04.260
a new kind of beverage took the stage.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:07.940
It wasn't a new shape
or a color or flavor.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:12.940
No, this was diet soda and it was awesome.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:16.400
With fewer calories and less sugar

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.800
diet soda promised to be

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.500
a healthier alternative to regular soda.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.540
But, like most promises in life

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.633
that sound too good to
be true, it probably is.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:33.630
Can you tell the difference

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.720
between a glass of regular and diet soda?

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.280
Turns out, neither can your body

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.370
and that's where the trouble starts.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.550
Until recently, everything we ate

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.960
contained some amount of calories.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.300
When we ate something sweet, for example,

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.500
the brain sent signals to our pancreas,

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.120
which started producing insulin

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:55.700
that stored the sugar molecules
in our cells for energy.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.050
So, when we drink diet soda,

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:01.810
the sweetness tricks our body
into thinking it's real sugar

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:04.600
but when those energy
packed calories don't arrive

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:07.240
the insulin has nothing to store.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:10.450
Scientists think that repeatedly
tricking our body this way

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:12.620
could explain why study after study

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.780
keeps finding the same thing.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:16.170
That drinking diet soda

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:19.160
is associated with metabolic syndrome.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.470
Metabolic syndrome is a mix of conditions

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:24.050
that includes increased blood pressure,

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.400
high blood sugar and weight gain

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.690
which can increase the risk of diabetes,

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:30.970
heart disease and stroke.

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:33.580
In fact, one study found
that diet soda drinkers

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.700
had a higher risk of stroke and dementia

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:37.910
than regular soda drinkers.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:42.380
And for another eight-year-long
study, between 1979 and 1988

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:44.690
participants who started
out at a normal weight

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:47.910
and drank an average of
21 diet beverages a week

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:51.280
faced double the risk of
becoming overweight or obese

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:52.490
by the end of the study

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:55.950
compared to people who avoided
diet beverages completely.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.590
And while drinking diet soda
with the meal may sound like

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:02.190
a tasty calorie free
alternative to plain water,

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:04.630
the growing body of
research is starting to find

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:07.120
that this may be the
worse time to drink it

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.460
because the fake calories in the diet soda

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:11.360
could ultimately disrupt how many

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.940
of the real calories we metabolize,

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:16.400
potentially leaving excess calories behind

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.640
that we then store as fat.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:20.360
Another issue could be the fact

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.600
that artificial sweeteners in diet sodas

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:26.350
can be 10s to 100s of
times sweeter than sugar.

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:28.750
So when we taste it, our brains anticipate

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.230
more calories than what we give it.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:34.370
It's like when you go to a
party expecting loads of food

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:38.430
and you end up with a handful
of veggies and vegan cheese.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:41.690
You're left unsatisfied and hangry.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:43.670
In the same way, artificial sweeteners

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:46.290
can leave our brains wanting more

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:49.000
which studies have shown
leads to increased appetite

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.646
and potential weight gain in
fruit flies, mice, and humans.

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:55.610
So if the reason you're drinking diet soda

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:59.890
is to drop a few pounds,
maybe just stick to water.

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:02.550
Got any friends obsessed with diet soda?

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:05.253
Share this video with them
and thanks for watching.

